c/new-york/clinton-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids, April to May came in under 90% of normal in 33 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025, August to September fell to 56% of normal on the middle of the grids, and July to August hit 64%. Grid 29925 had its driest year in 1964 at 71% of normal.</p>"}
